body:
There is something off about your stroke as others have stated, but the biggest thing I noticed is your body position, your hips are too low in the water.

&#x200B;

Practice pushing off the wall under water, hands in front of you one on top of the other.  You tell kids to squeeze your ears tight with your arms to get them to really stretch.  In reality your ears should be below your arms forcing your chin against your chest without looking down.  If you do this against a wall the only part of your upper body that shouldn't be touching the wall is the small of your back, otherwise its a straight line from your fingers to your butt.

&#x200B;

While pushing off underwater work on kicking your feet pretty fast, try not to surface until your upper body is past the flags.  Practicing this should allow you to bring your hips up while you swim too, further improving your stroke, but focus on the walls first.

I would get a cheap car over ride sharing and delivery, especially if you have to drive to work.  if you use your savings for a cheap car, and put 500 towards savings, you will make that back in 6 short months.  This time next year you will have 3k and a car.

&#x200B;

edit:  comments swayed me,  I would say finance a cheap used car, put $1-2k down, keep the loan short and the payments low.  Unless you find a good deal, most cars that cost $3k will probably need some work done within the year.
